course: dictionary
lesson: 13788
title: Intrusion: coming in where you are not wanted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An intrusion is when someone or something comes into a place or situation where they are not wanted or allowed. Look at the clues around the word. «The fox's intrusion into the hen house woke the whole farm.» A fox is not wanted in a hen house, so an intrusion is a coming-in that should not happen.
explain: Intrusion can also mean not respecting someone's privacy. «Reading my diary without asking was an intrusion into my private life.» Private means something that belongs only to you. Clue words like diary and without asking tell you that the writer was not allowed to look.
explain: In science, an intrusion is different. «Geologists found an intrusion of hard rock inside the older rock.» Here the word means rock that pushed into other rock while it was still melted, then cooled and went hard. The clue is the word rock, not people.
fact: An intrusion is when someone comes where they are not wanted or allowed.
fact: Intrusion into someone's private life means not respecting their privacy.
fact: In science, an intrusion is rock that pushed into other rock while it was melted.
fact: «Intrusion» is a noun, so you can say an intrusion, or intrusions.
fact: Use context clues: look for words like not wanted, private or rock to find which meaning fits.
exercise: «The noisy drone was an intrusion on our quiet picnic.» What does intrusion mean here? | A nice surprise | *Something coming in where it is not wanted | Leaving a place in a hurry | A tasty lunch
exercise: «Reading her diary without asking was an intrusion into her private life.» What does this show? | *Not respecting her privacy | Being a very good friend | Writing a story | Forgetting a birthday
exercise: «The grey rock was an intrusion: hot melted rock had pushed into the older rock and then cooled.» Which meaning fits in science? | A hole dug by a digger | *Rock that pushed into other rock while it was melted | A stone rolling down a hill | A layer of soft mud on a beach
test: «Nobody had invited the dog, so its sudden intrusion into the party surprised everyone.» Why was it an intrusion? | It was a very quiet walk | It was tired from running | *It was not wanted or allowed there | It was wanted and invited
test: «Scientists studied the intrusion of pale rock that had pushed into the dark stone.» Which subject studies rock like this? | Music | Maths | *Geology | Cooking
exam: Which is an example of intrusion into someone's private life? | Helping a neighbour carry shopping | Writing a thank-you note | Sharing a joke with a friend | *Reading a friend's private messages without asking
